   "road": "{\"name\":\"Chilliwack Lake Road + Depot Creek Road (BC) — same access used for the South Side route, from which this traverse is usually launched\",\"status\":\"Paved to Chilliwack Lake (~25 mi), then rough pothole-prone gravel to the Depot Creek Road fork at 32.6 mi; Depot Creek Road itself washed out beyond roughly 0.8-1.6 mi\",\"driveNote\":\"See the South Side route's Depot Creek approach; this traverse is done as a link, not from the road directly.\",\"seasonalGate\":null}",
   "overview": "A high, mostly Class 2/3 ridge-crest traverse directly connecting the summits of Mount Rahm and Mount Custer, with one short Class 4 gully bypassing an unclimbable arête near Custer's summit block.",
